# Build context for deploy/Dockerfile.* (context = repository root). Keep the context small and free of
# anything that must never reach an image: dependencies (installed in the image from the lockfile),
# VCS data, documents, environment files, credentials and local tooling.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log

.git
.github
.claude
.superpowers
.worktrees
worktrees
docs
LEIA-ME.md
CLAUDE.md
skills-lock.json

# Environment and secrets: never in an image (Sankhya and database values come from the runtime environment).
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
credentials
secrets
.sankhya-raw

# Local artifacts
**/*.dump
**/*.backup
**/*.sql.gz
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
apps/mobile

# Deployment files are not part of any image, except what Dockerfile.web copies (deploy/nginx).
deploy/*
!deploy/nginx
